==Personal life==
Bailey is married to Cindy Stortzum,<ref name="Announcement"/><ref>{{Cite news |date=2022-06-30 |title=Who is Darren Bailey wife Cindy Stortzum? |work=Bareillyinfo |url=https://bareillycollege.org/who-is-darren-bailey-wife-cindy-stortzum-wiki-biography-age-instagram/ |access-date=2022-07-04 |archive-date=June 26, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220626193214/https://bareillycollege.org/who-is-darren-bailey-wife-cindy-stortzum-wiki-biography-age-instagram/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> and they have four children and multiple grandchildren.<ref name="101stILGA2"/> He owns a [[family farm]].<ref name="101stILGA2"/> Bailey and his wife run a private Christian school.<ref name="GovernorRun"/>

In 2022, a man was arrested for making violent threats against Bailey, claiming he was going to "skin [Bailey] alive".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rose |first=Andy |date=2022-11-03 |title=Chicago man accused of leaving voicemail with death threats at office of Republican candidate for governor {{!}} CNN Politics |url=https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/03/politics/scott-lennox-death-threat-darren-bailey/index.html |access-date=2023-07-04 |website=CNN |language=en}}</ref>

In 2025, Bailey's son Zachary, his daughter-in-law Kelsey, and two of their three children, Vada Rose and Samuel, were killed in a helicopter crash in Montana.<ref>{{cite web |title=4 family members of Illinois governor candidate killed in Montana helicopter crash, campaign says |url=https://apnews.com/article/darren-bailey-family-helicopter-crash-75826f7a22c45f6e948f4f2200596462 |website=The Associated Press |access-date=October 23, 2025 |date=October 23, 2025}}</ref>

